A||N||16||FieroJoe||Factory pinstriping question||||1||
Z||000000||FieroJoe||03-28-2001||11:08 PM||||I am pretty sure that the pinstriping on my 87 coupe is factory.  I have 3 thin stripes along the upper part of the panels, and then a 5 or 6 stripe "gradient" effect on the bottom, where the GT ground effects would be.  It fades from red to gray.<P>Are these factory?  I have always wondered, as I have never seen them on another Fiero.<P>Does it mean anything special?  Like a special option or something?<BR><P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-29-2001||12:29 AM||||I don't believe there was any factory striping for the Fieros. Might have been done at the dealer or the former owner, (unless you are the first!)||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||03-29-2001||05:17 AM||||dealer do lots of pinstriping before the cars ever sold the first time. I know because I do it for a few around here. Ive never seen a Fiero with factory stripes. Someone here can run a search of some kind to see if it was even offered as a factory option.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||03-29-2001||05:50 AM||||I have an black 85 GT that has red and white pinstriping. Paint, not vinyl. I have seen two others with identical striping. If the paint on the car were good it would be a nice tasteful job.<BR>It is hand brushed and due to fading the brush strokes can be seen and near the left rear it is signed. I,ll look later for the name.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ferg||03-29-2001||11:07 AM||||here's a pic of the graphics applied to my car. We got the car used and have no idea if it's original. <P>The graphic is silver to match the ground effects and has small round holes to fade the red.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_fiero_rear_resized.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||03-29-2001||11:19 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by ferg:<BR>[B]here's a pic of the graphics applied to my car. We got the car used and have no idea if it's original. <P>The graphic is silver to match the ground effects and has small round holes to fade the red.<P><BR>No, that an aftermarket pattern from 3M, not available anymore. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||03-29-2001||11:42 AM||||Here is a portion of the stripping on the 85 GT with the siniture cloned in. It,s raining and I can't get a photo of the whole car because of glare. However this is representative.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/psgt.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroJoe||03-29-2001||11:46 AM||||Well, I was planning on taking it off for the repaint whether it was stock or not.  The orignial owner must have put it on.  I am the 3rd owner.<P>Its going to be a pain though to get it off.  I wasnt planning on spending $50 for one of those "drill powered erasers", so I am going to go very carefully with a razor blade and try not to gouge the plastic too much.<P>Any other suggestions?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Wolfhound||03-29-2001||12:00 PM||||Joe, Try taking a single edge razor blade and gently pull across the top side of the strip, just enough to break the edge seal. Spray with WD40. This will hold a little of the WD40 and allow it to loosen the adhesive. Wait about 2 or 3 minnets and repeat. Do it a panel at a time.<BR>Works for bumper stickers!||||reg||1
Z||000009||FieroJoe||03-29-2001||02:20 PM||||I will be staying away from greasy things like that.  Though there are solvents in WD-40, there are also oils.  Becuase I am repainting, I dont want any stray oil from the wd-40 that wasnt cleaned up with the prep-sol to come out while painting and ruin the finish.  Good idea though.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wolfhound||04-03-2001||05:01 PM||||Looking at RPO Codes today and saw:<BR> <BR>(D90)Stripping, front, side, Rear<P>Went out and checked the 85GT. It has that RPO Code, It is factory.||||reg||14
Z||000011||hugh||04-03-2001||07:55 PM||||Use a hair drier to soften the decal and the glue.Start at one end and slowly peel while using the drier.||||reg||1
Z||000012||rogergarrison||04-03-2001||08:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Wolfhound:<BR><B>Looking at RPO Codes today and saw:<BR> <BR>(D90)Stripping, front, side, Rear<P>Went out and checked the 85GT. It has that RPO Code, It is factory.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>I think youll find that thats the RPO code for the lower color (stripe) I have never seen a Fiero with a factory applied pinstripe. Maybe one of the factory gurus can enlighten us for sure.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||AusFiero||04-05-2001||10:22 AM||||Yep use the hair dryer..and a razor carefully. Turpentine or thinners will get any other glue off.||||reg||1
Z||000014||LZeitgeist||04-06-2001||09:14 AM||||Roger - <P>Does that include the Indys? I know the door decals were included in the trunk to be installed by the dealer for the owner if they wanted, but what about the red gradient striping? Was that a factory installation, or did the dealer do that, too? (Always been curious about that...)||||reg||1
Z||000015||rogergarrison||04-06-2001||12:44 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>Roger - <P>Does that include the Indys? I know the door decals were included in the trunk to be installed by the dealer for the owner if they wanted, but what about the red gradient striping? Was that a factory installation, or did the dealer do that, too? (Always been curious about that...)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Im sorry LZ, I dont know about the Indys, Id have to check one close up sometime. They may have had some special striping, but notta one of the reg ones ive seen have had any except the 'Formula' logo on the formulas. One way to tell is if all the Indys have the same stripe, then pretty good bet is was OEM.<P><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||FieroJoe||04-06-2001||06:52 PM||||Well, be it factory or not, its all gone right now.  My dad and I worked on it all day today and have already started to sand.  Here is a pic of it this morning after I washed it with dish soap to get all the wax and crap off it.  I think it will look much cleaner and overall better once it is repainted without the pinstriping.  You can see the stripes in my sig pic.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P1010005.jpg"> ||||reg||1
